SecureDKIM is a high-performance RFC 6376 DKIM signing and verification
milter written in Zig. It integrates with Postfix via the milter protocol
(v6) to sign outbound mail and verify inbound DKIM signatures.

Features:
- DKIM signing (RSA-SHA256, Ed25519-SHA256)
- DKIM verification with DNS public key lookup
- Header and body canonicalization (simple, relaxed)
- SigningTable/KeyTable for multi-domain support
- Single-domain shorthand config for simple deployments
- Sign/verify/both modes per listener
- Thread-per-core worker pool with kqueue I/O multiplexing
- Authentication-Results header generation (RFC 8601)
